# Vren, the Relentless: "If a creature an opponent controls would die, exile it instead" (CR 614.1a) and, at the beginning of each
# end step, X Rat tokens where X is the number of creatures exiled under the opponents' control this turn. Bot1 casts Vren on
# turn 1 (Sapphire, Jet and a Black Lotus), Bot2 plays Llanowar Elves, and on turn 3 Bot1 bolts it: it is exiled rather than put into the
# graveyard (so nothing in Bot2's graveyard), and in the end step one Rat is created. Vren is itself a Rat, so the token is 1/1 +1/+1 for
# the one other Rat = 2/2, while Vren stays 3/4. On Bot2's turn-4 end step nothing was exiled that turn, so no second token.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Vren, the Relentless
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x2
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x15

[Actions]
